# 0006. blink.cmp for completion

- Status: Accepted
- Date: 2026-11-07

Completion is one plugin, blink.cmp, with a prebuilt native fuzzy matcher, replacing nvim-cmp
and its seven helpers.

## Technical details
- **Problem**: completion was nvim-cmp plus cmp-nvim-lsp, -buffer, -path, -cmdline,
  cmp_luasnip, LuaSnip and lspkind; it was configured twice and lspkind icons never showed.
- **Spec** (`lua/plugins/coding.lua`): `saghen/blink.cmp`, `version = "1.*"` (release tags ship
  the prebuilt matcher, no Rust toolchain), loaded on `InsertEnter`/`CmdlineEnter`, snippets
  from friendly-snippets.
- **Keys** (`preset = "none"`, same keys as before): `<C-n>`/`<C-p>` show and select,
  `<CR>` accept, `<C-Space>` docs, `<C-e>` hide, `<C-b>`/`<C-f>` scroll docs, `<C-l>`/`<C-h>`
  snippet jumps, `<C-k>` signature. `<Tab>` stays free for Copilot.
- **Look**: rounded menu without scrollbar, columns kind icon / label / kind (icons and kinds
  hidden on the `:` line), docs auto-shown after 250 ms, signature help on, ghost text off
  (Copilot draws its own), first item preselected without auto-insert.
- **Sources**: `lsp`, `path`, `snippets`, `buffer`; Lua adds `lazydev` (score +100) for the
  Neovim API; sql/mysql/plsql use `dadbod` (vim-dadbod-completion). Cmdline completion on
  `:` and `/` with the `cmdline` preset.
- **Fuzzy matcher**: `implementation = "prefer_rust_with_warning"`. `make sync`/`make update`
  run `scripts/blink-fuzzy.lua`, which loads blink and waits up to 90 s for the matcher to
  become `rust`; if it can't be fetched, completion uses the slower Lua matcher and the
  script only warns (it fails only if the config itself didn't load).
- **LSP**: blink provides the capabilities for every server
  ([0004](0004-lsp-through-mason-and-native-vim-lsp.adr)).
- **Consequences**: one plugin instead of eight; typo-tolerant matching; docs and signature
  help built in. The matcher is a binary fetched per machine.

## Technologies and alternatives
- Involved: blink.cmp, friendly-snippets, lazydev.nvim, vim-dadbod-completion, copilot.vim.
- Alternatives: keep nvim-cmp and fix its config: eight plugins to keep in step.
